catching goods include silver accessories, ceramics, handmade soaps, artisanal cutting boards, wood crafts, and paintings. The best selling items include bowls of hot soup with rice, pancakes made of mung beans or seafood and scallions, and pan-fried seasoned","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gwangju","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Gwangju_Dong-gu_Election_Commission.jpg/1280px-Gwangju_Dong-gu_Election_Commission.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Gwangju_Dong-gu_Election_Commission.jpg/500px-Gwangju_Dong-gu_Election_Commission.jpg","w":1200,"h":675,"author":"Neoalpha","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gwangju_Dong-gu_Election_Commission.jpg"}},{"id":"gwangju_jeungsimsa_temple","areaId":"gwangju","name":"Jeungsimsa Temple","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":35.1219,"lng":126.9722},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"gwangju_jeungsimsa_temple","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["jeungsimsatemple","gwangju"],"summary":"Jeungsimsa Temple, one of Gwangju’s main Buddhist temples, is located at the western foot of Mudeungsan Mountain. Important cultural artifacts are preserved on the grounds. Climbing up the temple is quite easy. You can walk along the trail with an atmosphere in a quiet stillness. Jeungsimsa operates temple stay programs for tourists.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gwangju","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/%EC%A6%9D%EC%8B%AC%EC%82%AC_%EC%A0%84%EA%B2%BD.JPG/1280px-%EC%A6%9D%EC%8B%AC%EC%82%AC_%EC%A0%84%EA%B2%BD.JPG","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/%EC%A6%9D%EC%8B%AC%EC%82%AC_%EC%A0%84%EA%B2%BD.JPG/500px-%EC%A6%9D%EC%8B%AC%EC%82%AC_%EC%A0%84%EA%B2%BD.JPG","w":1200,"h":800,"author":"Dalgial","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EC%A6%9D%EC%8B%AC%EC%82%AC_%EC%A0%84%EA%B2%BD.JPG"}},{"id":"gwangju_gwangju_confucian_school","areaId":"gwangju","name":"Gwangju Confucian School","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":35.1458,"lng":126.9093},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"gwangju_gwangju_confucian_school","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["gwangjuconfucianschool","gwangju"],"summary":"The Gwangju Confucian School, which played a key role in Confucian education during the Joseon Dynasty (1329–1910) and served as a kind of national university at the time, today offers a “Confucian university” program through which participants can experience diverse aspects of traditional culture.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gwangju","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Gwangju_Hyanggyo_in_Hanam_City.jpg/1280px-Gwangju_Hyanggyo_in_Hanam_City.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Gwangju_Hyanggyo_in_Hanam_City.jpg/500px-Gwangju_Hyanggyo_in_Hanam_City.jpg","w":1200,"h":675,"author":"Qkqhrhkdtn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gwangju_Hyanggyo_in_Hanam_City.jpg"}},{"id":"gwangju_wv_the_traditional_culture_center","areaId":"gwangju","name":"The Traditional Culture Center","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":35.1336,"lng":126.9521},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"gwangju_wv_the_traditional_culture_center","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["thetraditionalculturecenter","gwangju"],"summary":"The center is near the entrance of Jeungsimsa Temple, at the foot of Mudeungsan Mountain. At the center, masters who have been designated as intangible cultural properties teach the public about traditional culture: Pansori (traditional Korean folk opera); Janggu (traditional drumming technique); Gayageum (traditional Korean zither). Performances are also held to demonstrate such elements of tradi","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gwangju"},{"id":"gwangju_yangdong_market","areaId":"gwangju","name":"Yangdong Market","category":"market","tags":["markets","food"],"location":{"lat":35.154,"lng":126.901},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"gwangju_yangdong_market","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["yangdongmarket","gwangju"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},null],"note":"Closed Sun; Typical hours — check the official site"},"bestLight":"morning","summary":"Since 2005, the river area has been undergoing a surprising facelift, stretching from Gwangju's most famous food, clothing and furniture market, Yangdong Market, all the way out of the city in a southeasterly direction. The river edge is beautifully lit at night, and with its colored lights and shopping areas nearby, is rapidly becoming a symbol of Gwangju - the City of Light and Culture.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gwangju"},{"id":"gwangju_wv_gwangju_student_independence_movement_memorial_h","areaId":"gwangju","name":"Gwangju Student Independence Movement Memorial Hall","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":35.1405,"lng":126.8653},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"gwangju_wv_gwangju_student_independence_movement_memorial_h","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://gsim.gen.go.kr/en/index.php","official":true}],"signa